		{"id":"7e70fc4b27c78efd","type":"text","text":"The idea of wearing a skull is considered evocative and pervasive among those who still live upon the palms of the Dactyloi, the forest-marooned tribes who now stand defiant against the rising of man above those who spawned him. To wear a skull over a living head is to become one with another's death, a daring demonstration of life and death as a confluence. The ways this tradition is practiced varies depending on the cult.\n\nSkull Priests have taken a vow of silence and don't speak, except in gestures.","x":840,"y":-220,"width":511,"height":280}
